#📸 Instagram Clone Web Application

This is a practice-based Instagram Clone Web Application built to improve my frontend development skills. 🚀

⚠️ Note: This project is created for learning and practice purposes only. It is not a complete or real Instagram application.

📖 About the Project

The main purpose of this project is to understand and practice modern frontend development concepts such as React.js, React Hooks, reusable components, dynamic data rendering, and UI design.

The project provides an Instagram-like user interface where users can view account details, profile photos, and reels. 👤📱

For demonstration purposes, the project contains a limited list of users and reels. The user accounts and photos shown in the application are only used for practice and demonstration. 🎭

🛠️ Technologies Used

🧱 HTML – Used to create the basic structure of the application.

🎨 CSS – Used for styling and creating an attractive Instagram-like design.

⚡ JavaScript – Used to add functionality and interactions.

⚛️ React.js – Used to build the user interface with reusable components.

🚀 Vite – Used to create and run the React project efficiently.

🪝 React Hooks – Used to manage state and component behavior.

✨ Main Features

📱 Instagram-like user interface

👤 Multiple user account details

🖼️ Random user profile photos

🎬 Reels component

🔄 Dynamic content rendering

🧩 Reusable React components

🪝 React Hooks implementation


🎯 Project Purpose

This project was developed mainly for practice and learning. It helped me understand how to build a frontend application using React.js and Vite, manage data using React Hooks, and create reusable components.

📌 Note: The number of users and reels is intentionally limited because this is a practice project and not a production-level application.
